+/** PASS 8 · THE PAGE'S OWN NAMES ON PAINT (the pass-7 critic's gap 4). `.rp-name` is the ruled
+ *  page's central text, `--color-muted-foreground` (#737373) in Fraunces 800 at φ, and no row
+ *  photographed it. The glyph population through the chair's ONE probe (G1–G5 at the 4.5 floor,
+ *  its G3 bound per payload, both themes), with its eight text plants run in the same page, each
+ *  RED. The names read a core median of 4.659 light / 7.681 dark in both engines, with 20–25 %
+ *  of the population under 4.5 in light — an antialiasing fraction, not the ink's: at
+ *  `--color-foreground` the same names keep 10–24 % under (their full-ink median 19.451). The ink
+ *  is the page's design and is NOT raised here; what it loses to the fold's page is written into
+ *  T9-B13's caption (the names at 4.659 / 7.681 against `s10`'s 19.451 / 15.839). */
+test.describe("the ruled page's own names are painted and seen (390×844 coarse, DPR 2)", () => {
