+/* ── §6.5 · THE MEASURED TOKENS ARE REGISTERED — PROVISIONAL, THE LEADER'S TO LAND ─────────
+   The chair's wave-wide ruling: every token whose value is MEASURED from a live box and
+   published by script (`--card-pad-t`, `--card-foot-h`, `--masthead-foot`, `--pin-band`, the
+   motion rungs) carries an `@property` registration with an `initial-value`, and consumers
+   then write `var(--x)` with NO fallback — so an absent publisher fails at computed-value
+   time and a born-RED row that deletes the publisher catches it, instead of a `, 0px` that
+   quietly paints a wrong-but-plausible layout. §10's LEADER (CTRL-FACE, taking TAPE's) lands that block
+   once, for the whole wave.
+
+   THIS IS NOT THAT BLOCK. It is the three rows CTRL-RULE consumes, copied row-for-row from
+   the leader's (CTRL-FACE, pass 4, `wf_f72f3b5a-83a-33` index.css:205–224, whose clauses —
+   first static sheet, `inherits: true`, an absolute initial — it inherits) so the strikes can
+   be MEASURED on this tree. AT THE FOLD THESE ROWS ARE DELETED and the leader's block stands.
+   Their consumers, named: `--card-pad-t` → W2's fold sentinel (`scene.css`
+   `.controls-card::before`, ×4; the margin pin reads `top: 0` and spends none of it);
+   `--card-foot-h` → the two card caps (`scene.css` desk + dock); `--card-pad-x` → `.card-foot`.
+   Every one is read bare. The `0px` initial collapses what it feeds (the sentinel's solid band,
+   the foot's inset, the cap's give-back), which is the leader's argument for it. */
+@property --card-pad-t {
+  syntax: "<length>";
+  inherits: true;
+  initial-value: 0px;
+}
+
+@property --card-foot-h {
+  syntax: "<length>";
+  inherits: true;
+  initial-value: 0px;
+}
+
+@property --card-pad-x {
+  syntax: "<length>";
+  inherits: true;
+  initial-value: 0px;
+}
+
+/* Pass 5 (W2 §2.4, the charter's row 2) — two rows PROPOSED for the leader's block, in the
+   `--masthead-foot` sibling form. `--toggle-foot` is DERIVED, not published: the celestial's
+   hit box is drawn from three `.page-root` tokens (`App.vue`), so its foot is written there
+   from the same three and cannot drift from the box it names. `--card-head-clear` is the
+   panel's (`GameControlPanel.vue`, `publishHeadClear`): the page's first line against that
+   foot. `0px` fails visibly: the first line rides back under the toggle and §2.4 reds. */
+/* Pass 6 (the charter's row 2) — W2 §2.5's publisher, taken from CTRL-TAPE's tree with its
+   registration in the same form (`App.vue` `publishMastheadFoot`; the leader registers the same
+   name). Consumed bare by `scene.css`'s `--sheet-chrome`. `0px` collapses the derivation to its
+   floor, and the 390×844 fine crossing row (`zone-grammar.spec.ts`) reds on exactly that. */
+@property --masthead-foot {
+  syntax: "<length>";
+  inherits: true;
+  initial-value: 0px;
+}
+
+@property --toggle-foot {
+  syntax: "<length>";
+  inherits: true;
+  initial-value: 0px;
+}
+
+/* Pass 8 (the charter's row 7) — the celestial's hover bound, ONE writer: this registration's
+   initial value. `DarkModeToggle.vue` scales by it on hover and `App.vue`'s `--toggle-foot`
+   names the reach it buys; before this, 1.08 was spelled at the hover and its half (0.54) in
+   the foot, a gated duplicate. PROPOSED for the leader's block with the rows above. */
+@property --toggle-reach {
+  syntax: "<number>";
+  inherits: true;
+  initial-value: 1.08;
+}
+
+@property --card-head-clear {
+  syntax: "<length>";
+  inherits: true;
+  initial-value: 0px;
+}
